 The route list below is the database-backed route set registered by `cmd/home` through `WithDatabaseManagement`.
 
+## Metadata-only diagnostics
+
+`CLIPROXY_DIAGNOSTICS_METADATA_ONLY=1` opts Home into a strict usage projection.
+It drops request-log pushes and removes failure bodies, client headers, unknown
+payload fields and raw client keys before scheduler ingestion, queues, fallback
+logs and database writes. Usage keeps a SHA-256 key reference for attribution;
+that reference cannot authenticate. Nodes sending a precomputed reference send
+matching `api_key` and `api_key_fingerprint` fields.
+
+Canonical UUID session IDs remain available for exact request-to-usage lookup.
+Home drops free-form session text. Nodes project custom session text to an
+opaque UUID before diagnostics retain it. Parent session text is omitted.
+
+The PostgreSQL old-writer guard installs before listeners open. The immutable
+`diagnostics_metadata_only_v1_1_6` data step audits and purges historical rows after
+Home starts serving. Each five-second transaction processes at most 100 rows,
+committing its audit counts, cleanup and cursor together. A failed batch emits
+only numeric retry metadata and retries with backoff without stopping serving.
+Other historical backfills yield to this audit; new usage and billing continue.
+
+The private `home_data_migration_audit_key` table retains distinct affected key
+IDs and one-way fingerprints for unknown keys. Runtime logs contain progress,
+retry and completion counts only. Completion is claimed once; the committed
+receipt remains available if the process dies before the line reaches logs.
+Authentication credentials, existing billing and usage totals, and the separate
+replay KV store are unchanged. Backups retain older copies until normal expiry.
+
 ## Authentication
 
 Management routes under `/v8/management/*` and `/v0/management/*` require a management key. The exception is `GET/POST /v8/management/oauth/callback`: it validates a pending OAuth `state` without the management-key middleware. Availability checks still apply, so a disabled Management API also disables the v8 callback.
